<h1 id="s3"><span class="n">3</span>Choosing the kind of test</h1>
<figure>@@FIG:ug_decision@@
<figcaption><b>Figure 3-1.</b> Which recipe to follow.</figcaption></figure>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 3-1.</b> The four kinds of test</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:15%">Recipe</th><th>Use when</th><th style="width:22%">You write</th><th style="width:22%"><code>tests.list</code> line</th></tr>
<tr><td><a href="#s5">A — C only</a></td><td>the firmware can check everything itself (registers, interrupts, internal loopback)</td><td><code>firmware/tests/my_test.c</code></td><td><code>my_test  fw_test  my_test</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="#s6">B — C + UVM</a></td><td>the testbench must drive or check pins, clocks or timing, or act at a precise point in the firmware</td><td>the C file + a test class</td><td><code>my_test  my_test_cls  my_test</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="#s7">C — UVM only</a></td><td>bus-level tests: the testbench is the bus master (stub CPU); the CPU sleeps</td><td>a sequence + a test class</td><td><code>my_test  my_test_cls  idle</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="#s8">D — TB only</a></td><td>the testbench only observes the chip (clocks, pins after boot)</td><td>a test class</td><td><code>my_test  my_test_cls  idle</code></td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================================================================== 4 -->
<h1 id="s4"><span class="n">4</span>What happens when you run a test</h1>
<figure>@@FIG:ug_flow@@
<figcaption><b>Figure 4-1.</b> <code>uvm/sim/run.sh my_test</code>, step by step.</figcaption></figure>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 4-1.</b> Pass criteria</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:26%">Kind</th><th>The test passes when</th></tr>
<tr><td>C, C + UVM</td><td>the firmware writes PASSED (<code>main()</code> returned 0), the UVM test's own checks raise no error, and no checker in the environment reports an error</td></tr>
<tr><td>UVM only, TB only</td><td><code>test_body()</code> finishes and no UVM error was reported (the firmware <code>idle</code> never reports PASSED)</td></tr>
<tr><td>All</td><td>the log ends with <code>*** TEST PASSED ***</code>; <code>run.sh</code> prints <code>RESULT: PASSED</code></td></tr>
</table>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 4-2.</b> Time limits (in <code>titan_base_test</code>)</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Limit</th><th>Value</th><th>Message when exceeded</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>boot_timeout</code></td><td>10 ms from POR to IN_TEST</td><td><code>firmware never reached main()</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>test_timeout</code></td><td>20 ms from IN_TEST to the end of <code>test_body()</code></td><td><code>test body did not finish within ...</code></td></tr>
</table>
<p>Override either in your test's constructor if a test legitimately needs longer (e.g. <code>test_timeout = 40ms;</code>).</p>

<!-- ================================================================== 5 -->
<h1 id="s5"><span class="n">5</span>Recipe A — C-only test</h1>
<div class="recipe"><b class="h">EXAMPLE</b>Check that <code>delay_us(50)</code> really waits 50 µs, measured with the hardware timer.</div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">1</div><div class="sb"><h3>Write the C file</h3>
<p class="file">new file: <b>firmware/tests/my_timer_test.c</b></p>
<pre><code><span class="c">// my_timer_test — C-only example: delay_us() really waits that long.</span>
<span class="c">//</span>
<span class="c">// Test entry (uvm/sim/tests.list):  my_timer_test   fw_test   my_timer_test</span>

<span class="k">#include</span> <span class="s">"titan.h"</span>

<span class="k">int</span> main(<span class="k">void</span>) {
  timer_init_us();                         <span class="c">// rv_timer: 1 tick = 1 us</span>
  uint64_t t0 = timer_now_us();
  delay_us(50);
  uint32_t dt = (uint32_t)(timer_now_us() - t0);

  titan_printf(<span class="s">"my_timer_test: delay_us(50) took %u us\n"</span>, dt);
  CHECK(dt &gt;= 50 &amp;&amp; dt &lt; 60, <span class="s">"delay_us(50) took %u us"</span>, dt);
  <span class="k">return</span> 0;                                <span class="c">// 0 = PASSED</span>
}</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Include only <code>titan.h</code> (plus <code>regs/&lt;ip&gt;_regs.h</code> for direct register access).</li>
<li>Fail with <code>CHECK(cond, fmt, ...)</code>: it prints file, line and your message, then reports FAILED.</li>
<li>Return 0 to pass. Do not loop forever: the test would end only at the timeout.</li>
</ul></div></div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">2</div><div class="sb"><h3>Check it compiles</h3>
<pre><code>make -C firmware TEST=my_timer_test      <span class="c"># → firmware/build/my_timer_test/my_timer_test.hex</span></code></pre>
<p>Compiler warnings are errors (<code>-Werror</code>). The listing <code>build/my_timer_test/my_timer_test.dis</code> shows the code with source lines.</p></div></div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">3</div><div class="sb"><h3>Register the test</h3>
<p class="file">edit: <b>uvm/sim/tests.list</b> — one line, three columns: name, UVM test class, firmware</p>
<pre><code>my_timer_test       fw_test                 my_timer_test</code></pre>
<p><code>fw_test</code> is the generic UVM test for C-only tests: it waits for the firmware's PASSED/FAILED.</p></div></div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">4</div><div class="sb"><h3>Run it</h3>
<pre><code>uvm/sim/run.sh my_timer_test</code></pre>
<p>Expected lines in <code>uvm/sim/runs/my_timer_test/run.log</code>:</p>
<pre><code>UVM_INFO ... uvm_test_top.env.sw [SW] firmware status: IN_TEST (main() started, boot 1)
UVM_INFO ... uvm_test_top.env.sw [SW] my_timer_test: delay_us(50) took 50 us
UVM_INFO ... uvm_test_top.env.sw [SW] firmware status: PASSED
UVM_INFO ... uvm_test_top.env.scoreboard [FABRIC_SB] ... transactions matched host-&gt;device, 0 DECERR, 0 errors, 0 resets
UVM_INFO ... uvm_test_top [TEST] *** TEST PASSED ***</code></pre></div></div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">5</div><div class="sb"><h3>Document it and commit</h3>
<p>Add a section to <code>uvm/TESTS.md</code> and follow the checklist in §12.</p></div></div>

<!-- ================================================================== 6 -->
<h1 id="s6"><span class="n">6</span>Recipe B — C + UVM test</h1>
<div class="recipe"><b class="h">EXAMPLE</b>The firmware makes a 10 µs pulse on GPIO0; the testbench measures its width at the pad.</div>
<figure>@@FIG:ug_sync@@
<figcaption><b>Figure 6-1.</b> Firmware and testbench working together. <code>titan_sync(n)</code> tells the testbench "step <i>n</i> reached"; <code>env.sw.wait_sync(n)</code> blocks until it is.</figcaption></figure>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">1</div><div class="sb"><h3>Write the firmware half</h3>
<p class="file">new file: <b>firmware/tests/my_gpio_pulse.c</b></p>
<pre><code><span class="c">// my_gpio_pulse — C + UVM example: firmware makes a 10 us pulse on GPIO0,</span>
<span class="c">// the testbench measures it.</span>
<span class="c">//</span>
<span class="c">// Step 1 (titan_sync(1)): GPIO0 is an output, low; the pulse starts now.</span>
<span class="c">// Step 2 (titan_sync(2)): the pulse is over.</span>
<span class="c">// Keep the width in step with my_gpio_pulse_test (uvm/tests/titan_test_pkg.sv).</span>
<span class="c">//</span>
<span class="c">// Test entry:  my_gpio_pulse   my_gpio_pulse_test   my_gpio_pulse</span>

<span class="k">#include</span> <span class="s">"titan.h"</span>

<span class="k">#define</span> PULSE_US 10

<span class="k">int</span> main(<span class="k">void</span>) {
  timer_init_us();
  pinmux_connect_tb_gpios();               <span class="c">// GPIO[7:0] &lt;-&gt; pads IOB0..IOB7</span>
  gpio_write(0);
  gpio_set_oe(0x1);                        <span class="c">// drive GPIO0 only</span>

  titan_sync(1);
  gpio_write(1);
  delay_us(PULSE_US);
  gpio_write(0);
  titan_sync(2);
  <span class="k">return</span> 0;
}</code></pre></div></div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">2</div><div class="sb"><h3>Write the testbench half</h3>
<p class="file">edit: <b>uvm/tests/titan_test_pkg.sv</b> — add the class inside the package, before <code>endpackage</code></p>
<pre><code><span class="k">class</span> my_gpio_pulse_test <span class="k">extends</span> titan_base_test;
  `uvm_component_utils(my_gpio_pulse_test)
  <span class="k">function</span> <span class="k">new</span>(string name, uvm_component parent);
    <span class="k">super</span>.new(name, parent);
  <span class="k">endfunction</span>

  <span class="k">virtual</span> <span class="k">task</span> test_body();
    realtime t_rise, t_fall;
    env.sw.wait_sync(1);                           <span class="c">// firmware: "pulse starts now"</span>
    <span class="k">wait</span> (env.gpio.vif.pins[0] === 1'b1);
    t_rise = $realtime;
    <span class="k">wait</span> (env.gpio.vif.pins[0] === 1'b0);
    t_fall = $realtime;
    env.sw.wait_sync(2);                           <span class="c">// firmware: "pulse is over"</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> (t_fall - t_rise &lt; 10us || t_fall - t_rise &gt; 12us)
      `uvm_error(<span class="s">"TEST"</span>, $sformatf(<span class="s">"GPIO0 pulse was %0t, expected 10 us"</span>, t_fall - t_rise))
    <span class="k">else</span>
      `uvm_info(<span class="s">"TEST"</span>, $sformatf(<span class="s">"GPIO0 pulse %0t"</span>, t_fall - t_rise), UVM_LOW)
    <span class="k">super</span>.test_body();                             <span class="c">// wait for PASSED from the firmware</span>
  <span class="k">endtask</span>
<span class="k">endclass</span></code></pre>
<ul>
<li><code>`uvm_component_utils</code> registers the class so <code>+UVM_TESTNAME</code> can find it — without it the run stops with "test not found".</li>
<li><code>test_body()</code> starts after the firmware has written IN_TEST; the chip is booted and clocks are calibrated.</li>
<li>Call <code>super.test_body()</code> at the end so the test also waits for, and checks, the firmware's PASSED.</li>
</ul></div></div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">3</div><div class="sb"><h3>Register and run</h3>
<pre><code><span class="c"># uvm/sim/tests.list</span>
my_gpio_pulse       my_gpio_pulse_test      my_gpio_pulse

uvm/sim/run.sh my_gpio_pulse</code></pre></div></div>

<h2 id="s6-1"><span class="n">6.1</span>What the testbench can reach</h2>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 6-1.</b> Environment handles available inside a test (<code>env</code> is a <code>titan_env</code>)</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:34%">Handle</th><th>Use</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.sw.wait_sync(n)</code></td><td>block until the firmware calls <code>titan_sync(n)</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.sw.ev_done</code>, <code>env.sw.passed()</code>, <code>env.sw.n_boots</code></td><td>firmware finished / passed / how many times the chip booted</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.gpio.vif.pins[7:0]</code></td><td>values on pads IOB0–IOB7 (GPIO[7:0])</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.gpio.vif.drv_en[i]</code>, <code>env.gpio.vif.drv_val[i]</code></td><td>drive pad IOB<i>i</i> from the testbench (a GPIO input to the chip)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.gpio.values</code></td><td>queue of settled GPIO[7:0] values, in order</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.uart0.text</code></td><td>everything received from UART0 TX (1 Mbaud, 8N1)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.uart0.vif.rx</code></td><td>UART0 RX pin into the chip (idles high)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.clk.count_edges(name, window, n)</code>, <code>env.clk.measure_hz(name, window, hz)</code></td><td>clocks: <code>main io io_div2 io_div4 usb aon io_div4_peri io_div2_peri io_peri usb_peri</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>env.sim_master()</code></td><td>sequencer of the testbench AXI master (Recipe C)</td></tr>
</table>
<h2 id="s6-2"><span class="n">6.2</span>Passing data between the halves</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Firmware → testbench:</b> <code>titan_sync(n)</code> for "step reached"; log text with <code>titan_printf</code>; pins.</li>
<li><b>Testbench → firmware:</b> pins only (drive a GPIO input; the firmware polls it or takes an interrupt — see <code>fw_plic_gpio_irq</code>).</li>
<li><b>Shared constants</b> (pattern tables, expected strings, timings) exist twice, in C and in SV. Nothing links them at compile time: put a comment on both sides naming the other file.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ================================================================== 7 -->
<h1 id="s7"><span class="n">7</span>Recipe C — UVM-only test (stub CPU)</h1>
<div class="recipe"><b class="h">EXAMPLE</b>The testbench writes 16 words to main SRAM over AXI and reads them back. The CPU runs the <code>idle</code> firmware and stays asleep.</div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">1</div><div class="sb"><h3>Write the sequence and the test</h3>
<p class="file">edit: <b>uvm/tests/titan_test_pkg.sv</b></p>
<pre><code><span class="k">class</span> my_sram_pattern_seq <span class="k">extends</span> axi_test_seq;
  `uvm_object_utils(my_sram_pattern_seq)
  <span class="k">function</span> <span class="k">new</span>(string name = <span class="s">"my_sram_pattern_seq"</span>);
    <span class="k">super</span>.new(name);
  <span class="k">endfunction</span>

  <span class="k">virtual</span> <span class="k">task</span> body();
    <span class="k">bit</span> [31:0] base = 32'h1001_8000;               <span class="c">// above the firmware's data/stack</span>
    <span class="k">bit</span> [31:0] d;
    <span class="k">bit</span> [1:0]  r;
    <span class="k">for</span> (<span class="k">int</span> i = 0; i &lt; 16; i++) <span class="k">begin</span>
      write32(base + 4 * i, 32'hC0DE_0000 | i, r);
      check(r == AXI_OKAY, $sformatf(<span class="s">"write %0d: %s"</span>, i, resp_name(r)));
    <span class="k">end</span>
    <span class="k">for</span> (<span class="k">int</span> i = 0; i &lt; 16; i++) <span class="k">begin</span>
      read32(base + 4 * i, d, r);
      check(r == AXI_OKAY &amp;&amp; d == (32'hC0DE_0000 | i),
            $sformatf(<span class="s">"word %0d = 0x%08h %s"</span>, i, d, resp_name(r)));
    <span class="k">end</span>
  <span class="k">endtask</span>
<span class="k">endclass</span>

<span class="k">class</span> my_sram_pattern_test <span class="k">extends</span> axi_stub_cpu_test;
  `uvm_component_utils(my_sram_pattern_test)
  <span class="k">function</span> <span class="k">new</span>(string name, uvm_component parent);
    <span class="k">super</span>.new(name, parent);
  <span class="k">endfunction</span>
  <span class="k">virtual</span> <span class="k">function</span> axi_test_seq make_seq();
    <span class="k">return</span> my_sram_pattern_seq::type_id::create(<span class="s">"my_sram_pattern_seq"</span>);
  <span class="k">endfunction</span>
<span class="k">endclass</span></code></pre></div></div>

<div class="step"><div class="sn">2</div><div class="sb"><h3>Register and run</h3>
<pre><code><span class="c"># uvm/sim/tests.list — firmware is always 'idle' for UVM-only tests</span>
my_sram_pattern     my_sram_pattern_test    idle

uvm/sim/run.sh my_sram_pattern</code></pre>
<p><code>axi_stub_cpu_test</code> runs your sequence on the testbench master and fails the test if the sequence's <code>check()</code> counted any error.</p></div></div>

<h2 id="s7-1"><span class="n">7.1</span>Sequence helpers</h2>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 7-1.</b> Provided by <code>axi_base_seq</code> / <code>axi_test_seq</code></p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:44%">Call</th><th>Does</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>write32(addr, data, resp)</code></td><td>single 32-bit write; <code>resp</code> = BRESP</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>read32(addr, data, resp)</code></td><td>single 32-bit read</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>write(addr, data[$], strb[$], resp, len, size, burst, id)</code></td><td>burst write (<code>len</code> = beats − 1; <code>size</code> 0/1/2; <code>burst</code> <code>AXI_INCR</code>/<code>AXI_WRAP</code>/<code>AXI_FIXED</code>; <code>id</code> &lt; 16)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>read(addr, data[$], resp[$], len, size, burst, id)</code></td><td>burst read, one data and response per beat</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>check(ok, msg)</code></td><td>count and report an error when <code>ok</code> is 0</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>resp_name(r)</code>; <code>AXI_OKAY</code>, <code>AXI_SLVERR</code>, <code>AXI_DECERR</code></td><td>responses</td></tr>
</table>
<h2 id="s7-2"><span class="n">7.2</span>Rules for bus-level tests</h2>
<ul>
<li>Use main SRAM at <code>0x1001_0000</code> and above; the firmware's own data and stack occupy <code>0x1000_0000–0x1000_4FFF</code>.</li>
<li>Expect DECERR for unmapped addresses, SLVERR for registers an IP refuses. The scoreboard checks routing for you either way.</li>
<li>Bursts are split into single accesses by the IP's bridge; registers usually want single 32-bit accesses.</li>
<li>Atomic operations (ATOPs) are answered SLVERR before the crossbar and never reach an IP.</li>
<li>Do not touch flash (<code>0x2000_0000</code>) or the retention SRAM before initializing them: an uninitialized flash read stalls, an uninitialized SRAM read returns X.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ================================================================== 8 -->
<h1 id="s8"><span class="n">8</span>Recipe D — testbench-only test</h1>
<div class="recipe"><b class="h">EXAMPLE</b>Measure the 24 MHz peripheral clock after boot.</div>
<p class="file">edit: <b>uvm/tests/titan_test_pkg.sv</b></p>
<pre><code><span class="k">class</span> my_clk_check_test <span class="k">extends</span> titan_base_test;
  `uvm_component_utils(my_clk_check_test)
  <span class="k">function</span> <span class="k">new</span>(string name, uvm_component parent);
    <span class="k">super</span>.new(name, parent);
  <span class="k">endfunction</span>
  <span class="k">virtual</span> <span class="k">task</span> test_body();
    <span class="k">real</span> hz;
    env.clk.measure_hz(<span class="s">"io_div4"</span>, 20us, hz);
    <span class="k">if</span> (hz &lt; 23.5e6 || hz &gt; 24.5e6)
      `uvm_error(<span class="s">"TEST"</span>, $sformatf(<span class="s">"clk_io_div4 = %.3f MHz, expected 24"</span>, hz / 1e6))
  <span class="k">endtask</span>
<span class="k">endclass</span>

<span class="c">// uvm/sim/tests.list</span>
<span class="c">// my_clk_check        my_clk_check_test       idle</span></code></pre>
<p>Do <b>not</b> call <code>super.test_body()</code> here: it would wait for a PASSED the <code>idle</code> firmware never writes, and the test would time out.</p>

<!-- ================================================================== 9 -->
<h1 id="s9"><span class="n">9</span>Working with registers</h1>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 9-1.</b> Where to find register information</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:26%">You need</th><th>Find it in</th></tr>
<tr><td>Base address of an IP</td><td>C: <code>TOP_EARLGREY_&lt;IP&gt;_BASE_ADDR</code> in <code>firmware/include/top_earlgrey.h</code>; manual Table 4-1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register offset and fields</td><td><code>firmware/include/regs/&lt;ip&gt;_regs.h</code>: <code>&lt;IP&gt;_&lt;REG&gt;_REG_OFFSET</code>, <code>_BIT</code>, <code>_MASK</code>, <code>_OFFSET</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Reset values, field meaning</td><td>the IP's register description: <code>vendor/opentitan/hw/ip/&lt;ip&gt;/data/&lt;ip&gt;.hjson</code> (or <code>hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/&lt;ip&gt;/data/</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Interrupt ID of a peripheral</td><td><code>kTopEarlgreyPlicIrqId&lt;Ip&gt;&lt;Irq&gt;</code> in <code>top_earlgrey.h</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Pinmux indices</td><td><code>kTopEarlgreyPinmuxPeripheralIn*</code>, <code>kTopEarlgreyPinmuxOutsel*</code>, <code>kTopEarlgreyPinmuxMioOut*</code>, <code>kTopEarlgreyPinmuxInsel*</code></td></tr>
</table>
<div class="two">
<div><p class="file">C</p>
<pre><code><span class="k">#include</span> <span class="s">"regs/uart_regs.h"</span>
<span class="k">#include</span> <span class="s">"titan.h"</span>

uint32_t s = reg32_read(TOP_EARLGREY_UART0_BASE_ADDR,
                        UART_STATUS_REG_OFFSET);
CHECK(s &amp; BIT(UART_STATUS_TXIDLE_BIT), <span class="s">"tx busy"</span>);</code></pre></div>
<div><p class="file">UVM sequence</p>
<pre><code><span class="c">// uart0 STATUS = 0x4000_0000 + 0x14</span>
read32(32'h4000_0014, d, r);
check(r == AXI_OKAY &amp;&amp; d == 32'h3C,
      $sformatf(<span class="s">"STATUS = 0x%08h"</span>, d));</code></pre></div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b class="h">NOTE</b>Out of reset the pinmux connects no pad. A firmware test that uses UART0 or GPIO pins must call <code>pinmux_connect_uart0()</code> or <code>pinmux_connect_tb_gpios()</code> first.</div>

<!-- ================================================================== 10 -->
<h1 id="s10"><span class="n">10</span>Extending the environment</h1>
<h2 id="s10-1"><span class="n">10.1</span>A new firmware helper</h2>
<ol>
<li>Add the function to <code>firmware/lib/drivers.c</code> (include the IP's <code>regs/&lt;ip&gt;_regs.h</code> there).</li>
<li>Declare it in <code>firmware/include/titan.h</code>, in the drivers section.</li>
<li>Rebuild all firmware (<code>make -C firmware all</code>) — every test links the library.</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="s10-2"><span class="n">10.2</span>An interrupt handler</h2>
<p>Define <code>titan_isr_external()</code> (PLIC) or <code>titan_isr_timer()</code> in your test file; it overrides the default, which fails the test on any unexpected interrupt. Pattern for the PLIC: <code>id = plic_claim()</code> → clear the cause in the peripheral → <code>plic_complete(id)</code>. Model: <code>firmware/tests/plic_gpio_irq.c</code>.</p>
<h2 id="s10-3"><span class="n">10.3</span>A new pin-level agent (e.g. I2C, SPI)</h2>
<ol>
<li><code>uvm/agents/&lt;name&gt;_agent/&lt;name&gt;_if.sv</code> and <code>&lt;name&gt;_agent_pkg.sv</code> (model: <code>uart_agent</code>).</li>
<li>Add both files to <code>uvm/sim/uvm.f</code>, interface before package.</li>
<li>In <code>uvm/tb/tb_top.sv</code>: instantiate the interface, connect it to the pads (and remove those pads' pull-downs if you drive them), and put it into <code>uvm_config_db</code>.</li>
<li>In <code>uvm/env/titan_env_pkg.sv</code>: import the package, add the component to <code>titan_env</code>, create it in <code>build_phase</code>.</li>
<li>In firmware: route the peripheral to those pads with the pinmux.</li>
<li>Lint (§11.3) before the first simulation.</li>
</ol>

<!-- ================================================================== 11 -->
<h1 id="s11"><span class="n">11</span>Running and debugging your test</h1>
<h2 id="s11-1"><span class="n">11.1</span>Commands</h2>
<pre><code>uvm/sim/run.sh my_test                       <span class="c"># run</span>
uvm/sim/run.sh my_test --seed 7              <span class="c"># another seed</span>
uvm/sim/run.sh my_test --waves               <span class="c"># waves: simvision uvm/sim/runs/my_test/waves.shm &amp;</span>
uvm/sim/run.sh my_test --trace 0x40000014    <span class="c"># every AXI port one address crossed</span>
uvm/sim/run.sh my_test --verbosity UVM_HIGH  <span class="c"># every AXI transaction on every port</span>
uvm/sim/run.sh my_test --print               <span class="c"># show the commands only</span></code></pre>
<h2 id="s11-2"><span class="n">11.2</span>Reading the log</h2>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 11-1.</b> Log tags</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:18%">Tag</th><th>Source</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>[TB]</code></td><td>testbench top: which images were loaded</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[SW]</code></td><td>the firmware: its status, its log text, sync steps (at <code>UVM_MEDIUM</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[TEST]</code>, <code>[SEQ]</code></td><td>your UVM test and sequences</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[FABRIC_SB]</code></td><td>interconnect scoreboard: summary at the end, or an error</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[uart0]</code>, <code>[TRACE]</code></td><td>UART monitor lines; address trace</td></tr>
</table>
<h2 id="s11-3"><span class="n">11.3</span>Compile check without a simulator</h2>
<pre><code>uvm/sim/lint.py --top tb_top --uvm -D TITAN_SIM -D SIMULATION rtl/flist/rtl.f uvm/sim/uvm.f</code></pre>
<p>Finds syntax, type and port errors in about a minute. Run it after every SystemVerilog change.</p>
<h2 id="s11-4"><span class="n">11.4</span>Common problems</h2>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table 11-2.</b> Problems when adding a test</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:36%">Symptom</th><th>Cause and fix</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>test 'my_test' not in uvm/sim/tests.list</code></td><td>add the line (name, class, firmware)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>UVM_FATAL ... Requested test ... not found</code></td><td>the class is missing <code>`uvm_component_utils</code>, or is outside <code>titan_test_pkg</code>, or its name differs from <code>tests.list</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>make: ... No rule to make target 'tests/x.c'</code></td><td>the firmware column of <code>tests.list</code> does not match a file in <code>firmware/tests/</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>BUILD FAILED</code></td><td>run the lint; then <code>uvm/sim/runs/build/build.log</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>test body did not finish</code></td><td>usually a <code>wait_sync(n)</code> for a step the firmware never reaches (wrong number, or the firmware failed first: look for <code>[SW] CHECK FAILED</code> above)</td></tr>
<tr><td>UVM-only test times out</td><td><code>super.test_body()</code> called with <code>idle</code> firmware</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[SW] EXCEPTION mcause=5/7 mtval=...</code></td><td>load/store to an address no device owns (DECERR); <code>mtval</code> is the address</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[SW] unexpected ... interrupt</code></td><td>an interrupt is enabled but the test has no handler</td></tr>
<tr><td>pins never change</td><td>pinmux not connected, or output enable not set</td></tr>
<tr><td>the firmware change has no effect</td><td>you edited a different firmware than the one named in <code>tests.list</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>FABRIC_SB</code> errors</td><td>a real interconnect problem, or a transaction to a gated / uninitialized IP — see the manual §9</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================================================================== 12 -->
<h1 id="s12"><span class="n">12</span>Before you commit</h1>
<ul class="check">
<li>The test passes: <code>uvm/sim/run.sh my_test</code>, and with a second seed</li>
<li>It really checks something: temporarily break the expectation and see it fail</li>
<li>Shared constants are commented on both sides (C and SV)</li>
<li>The line is in <code>uvm/sim/tests.list</code> (only once it passes)</li>
<li>A section in <code>uvm/TESTS.md</code>: goal, method, pass criteria</li>
<li>The full regression is green: <code>uvm/sim/regress.sh</code></li>
<li>The documents are regenerated: <code>.venv/bin/python uvm/doc/gen_guide.py</code> (updates both HTML files' test lists)</li>
<li>Only <code>firmware/</code>, <code>uvm/</code> and the generated HTML changed: <code>git status</code></li>
</ul>
<pre><code>git checkout -b test/my_test                       <span class="c"># or work on main if that is the team's rule</span>
git add firmware/tests/my_test.c uvm/tests/titan_test_pkg.sv uvm/sim/tests.list uvm/TESTS.md *.html
git commit -m <span class="s">"Add my_test: &lt;what it verifies&gt;"</span>
git push -u origin test/my_test</code></pre>

<!-- ================================================================== A -->
<h1 id="sA"><span class="n">A</span>Firmware API reference</h1>
<p class="tcap"><b>Table A-1.</b> <code>firmware/include/titan.h</code></p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:44%">Function / macro</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>CHECK(cond, fmt, ...)</code></td><td>fail with file:line and message</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>titan_pass()</code>, <code>titan_fail()</code></td><td>end the test now</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>titan_printf(fmt, ...)</code>, <code>titan_puts(s)</code>, <code>titan_putc(c)</code></td><td>log text to the testbench (<code>%d %u %x %08x %c %s %p</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>titan_sync(n)</code></td><td>tell the testbench "step n reached"</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>reg32_read(base, off)</code>, <code>reg32_write(base, off, v)</code>, <code>reg32_write_field(...)</code>, <code>BIT(n)</code></td><td>register access</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>pinmux_connect_uart0()</code>, <code>pinmux_connect_tb_gpios()</code></td><td>connect UART0 (IOC4/IOC3) and GPIO[7:0] (IOB0–7) to the pads</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>uart_init(baud)</code>, <code>uart_putc</code>, <code>uart_puts</code>, <code>uart_flush</code></td><td>UART0</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>gpio_set_oe(mask)</code>, <code>gpio_write(v)</code>, <code>gpio_read()</code></td><td>GPIO</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>timer_init_us()</code>, <code>timer_now_us()</code>, <code>delay_us(us)</code>, <code>timer_set_deadline_us(t)</code>, <code>timer_irq_enable(on)</code>, <code>timer_irq_ack()</code></td><td>rv_timer (1 tick = 1 µs)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>irq_global_enable</code>, <code>irq_timer_enable</code>, <code>irq_external_enable</code></td><td>interrupt enables</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>plic_enable(id, prio)</code>, <code>plic_claim()</code>, <code>plic_complete(id)</code></td><td>PLIC</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>titan_isr_timer()</code>, <code>titan_isr_external()</code>, <code>titan_exception_handler()</code></td><td>define in a test to handle interrupts / exceptions</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>rstmgr_reset_info()</code>, <code>rstmgr_clear_reset_info()</code>, <code>rstmgr_request_sw_reset()</code></td><td>reset cause, software reset</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>pwrmgr_enable_reset_request(i)</code>, <code>clkmgr_peri_clock_enable(bit, on)</code>, <code>aon_wdog_start/stop</code></td><td>power, clock gating, watchdog</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>CSR_READ</code>, <code>CSR_WRITE</code>, <code>CSR_SET</code>, <code>CSR_CLEAR</code>, <code>wait_for_interrupt()</code></td><td>RISC-V CSRs, <code>wfi</code></td></tr>
</table>

